{# PL·A2 "Patrols today" — TODAY, NOT THE MONTH.

   Every number on this card is scoped to one day and compared with the same
   weekday a week ago, so none of them reconciles with the module's monthly KPI
   strip — and must not. The closing line says so out loud, with the month's own
   figures beside it, because a person who spots two different totals for
   "patrols" deserves to be told which question each answered.

   THE ONE THING THIS CARD CANNOT SAY is how many of the day's observations were
   filed as incidents. That is recorded by the incidents module on its own side
   and nothing here mirrors it, so the second clause of the design's line is an
   em dash rather than a number. #}
{% set pl = by.patrols %}
{% set t = pl.today %}
<div class="c" data-w="pl_today">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·A2</span>Patrols today<span class="src">· {{ t.day|date('D j M')|lower }} · vs {{ t.lastWeek|date('D j M')|lower }}</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by patrols"><i></i>patrols</span>

    <div class="grid g2 patrol-ao-pair">
        <div class="kpi">
            <b class="disp">{{ t.closed }}<em>closed</em></b>
            <span class="sub">{{ t.closed == t.closedLastWeek ? 'the same as' : (t.closed - t.closedLastWeek)|abs ~ (t.closed > t.closedLastWeek ? ' more than' : ' fewer than') }} last {{ t.lastWeek|date('l')|lower }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi hot">
            {# An em dash, never 0 km: a day of hand-logged patrols walked a
               distance nobody measured. #}
            {% if t.distanceKm is null %}
                <b class="disp">—</b>
                <span class="sub">no distance recorded today</span>
            {% else %}
                <b class="disp">{{ t.distanceKm|number_format }}<em>km</em></b>
                <span class="sub">{% if t.distanceKmLastWeek is null %}not recorded last {{ t.lastWeek|date('l')|lower }}{% else %}{{ (t.distanceKm - t.distanceKmLastWeek) >= 0 ? '+' : '−' }}{{ (t.distanceKm - t.distanceKmLastWeek)|abs|number_format }} km on last {{ t.lastWeek|date('l')|lower }}{% endif %}</span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Observations logged</span>
        <span class="mono patrol-ao-mono">{{ t.observations }} · <span class="fog">— filed as incidents</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">By type</span>
        <span class="mono patrol-ao-mono">{% for key, count in t.typeCounts %}{{ count }} {{ pl.types[key].label|default(key)|lower }}{{ not loop.last ? ' · ' }}{% endfor %}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Stations that patrolled</span>
        <span class="mono patrol-ao-mono">{{ t.stations|length ? t.stations|join(', ') : 'none recorded' }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Still out</span>
        <span class="mono w patrol-ao-mono">{{ t.stillOut }}{% if t.stillOutRefs|length %} · {{ t.stillOutRefs|join(', ') }}{% endif %}</span>
    </div>

    <div class="use">This month’s {{ t.monthCount|number_format }} patrols{% if t.monthDistanceKm is not null %} and {{ t.monthDistanceKm|number_format }} km{% endif %} live on the module. Today’s numbers deliberately do not add up to them — different question, different window. Whether an observation has been filed as an incident is recorded by the incidents module, not on this side, so this card does not count it.</div>
</div>
